[45.175242, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m2\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[45.175819, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe directory contains only the 10,000-line test file. I need to build the serial algorithm and a Berkeley UPC parallel version. First, I'll check system \r\narchitecture and compiler availability, then install/configure Berkeley UPC as specified.\r\n\r\n```\r\nuname -a; cat /etc/os-release | head -5; echo '---compilers---'; which gcc g++ make wget curl tar 2>/dev/null; gcc --version | head -1; echo '---existing \r\nupc---'; ls -d /usr/local/upc* /usr/local/bin/upc* 2>/dev/null || true; echo '---deps---'; dpkg -l | grep -E 'libc6-dev|make|wget' | head\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[45.176108, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠙\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[45.195175, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[45.19551, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\nLinux f7d7a33ec365 6.17.0-1014-nvidia #14-Ubuntu SMP PREEMPT_DYNAMIC Tue Mar 17 19:01:40 UTC 2026 aarch64 aarch64 aarch64 GNU/Linux\r\nPRETTY_NAME=\"Ubuntu 24.04.2 LTS\"\r\nNAME=\"Ubuntu\"\r\nVERSION_ID=\"24.04\"\r\nVERSION=\"24.04.2 LTS (Noble Numbat)\"\r\nVERSION_CODENAME=noble\r\n---compilers---\r\n/usr/bin/gcc\r\n/usr/bin/g++\r\n/usr/bin/make\r\n/usr/bin/wget\r\n/usr/bin/curl\r\n/usr/bin/tar\r\ngcc (Ubuntu 13.3.0-6ubuntu2~24.04.1) 13.3.0\r\n---existing upc---\r\n---deps---\r\nii  libc6-dev:arm64                 2.39-0ubuntu8.9                   arm64        GNU C Library: Development Libraries and Header Files\r\nii  make                            4.3-4.1build2                     arm64        utility for directing compilation\r\nii  wget                            1.21.4-1ubuntu4.5                 arm64        retrieves files from the web\r\n\r\n"]
