[55.487464, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m4\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[55.487862, "o", "\r\u001b[2KNow I'll verify how the forward/backward extensions map to edges and whether all graph links are internally consistent. This will determine the traversal rules.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app; python3 - <<'PY'\r\nfrom collections import defaultdict, Counter\r\nkmers={}\r\nwith open('test') as f:\r\n  for line in f:\r\n    k,e=line.rstrip('\\n').split('\\t')\r\n    kmers[k]=e\r\nprint('n',len(kmers))\r\nmissingR=Counter(); missingL=Counter(); both=0\r\nedges=[]\r\nfor k,e in kmers.items():\r\n    l,r=e\r\n    if r!='F':\r\n      succ=k[1:]+r\r\n      if succ not in kmers: missingR[(k,e)]=succ\r\n      else: edges.append((k,succ))\r\n    if l!='F':\r\n      pred=l+k[:-1]\r\n      if pred not in kmers: missingL[(k,e)]=pred\r\nprint('right ext edges',sum(1 for e in kmers.values() if e[1]!='F'),'missing',len(missingR))\r\nprint('left ext edges',sum(1 for e in kmers.values() if e[0]!='F'),'missing',len(missingL))\r\n# compare inferred edges sets: left link at Y should be edge X->Y where X=left(Y)+Y[:-1]\r\ninferred=set()\r\nfor k,e in kmers.items():\r\n    l,r=e\r\n    if l!='F': inferred.add((l+k[:-1],k))\r\ndirect=set(edges)\r\nprint('direct',len(direct),'inferred',len(inferred),'same',direct==inferred,'d-i',len(direct-inferred),'i-d',len(inferred-direct))\r\n# degrees\r\nind=Counter(); outd=Counter()\r\nfor a,b in direct:\r\n  outd[a]+=1; ind[b]+=1\r\nprint('outdeg',Counter(outd.values()),'indeg',Counter(ind.values()))\r\nprint('nodes with both0-ish',sum(1 for k in kmers if ind[k]==0 and outd[k]==0))\r\nprint('components/path starts')\r\nPY\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
