[279.614644, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe first serial run produced many fragmented contigs because the hash-chain link and the graph successor link shared one field. I'll separate them and rebuild.\r\n\r\n```\r\ncd /app\r\npython3 - <<'PY'\r\np='serial.c'\r\ns=open(p).read()\r\ns=s.replace('    int next;      /* successor node index, -1 if none */\\n', '    int hash_next;\\n    int next;      /* successor node index, -1 if none */\\n')\r\ns=s.replace('for (int p = buckets[b]; p >= 0; p = nodes[p].next) {', 'for (int p = buckets[b]; p >= 0; p = nodes[p].hash_next) {')\r\ns=s.replace('        nodes[n].next = buckets[b];\\n        buckets[b] = n;', '        nodes[n].hash_next = buckets[b];\\n        buckets[b] = n;')\r\ns=s.replace('            nodes[i].next = new_buckets[b];\\n            new_buckets[b] = i;', '            nodes[i].hash_next = new_buckets[b];\\n            \r\nnew_buckets[b] = i;')\r\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\r\nPY\r\ngrep -n 'hash_next\\|p = buckets\\|nodes\\[n\\]\\.next = buckets' serial.c | head -20\r\ngcc -O2 -Wall -Wextra -o serial serial.c && ./serial test && echo '--- result ---' && wc -l serial.out && awk '{print length($0)}' serial.out && head -3 \r\nserial.out\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[279.615017, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠴\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[279.748563, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[279.750172, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n11:    int hash_next;\r\n82:        for (int p = buckets[b]; p >= 0; p = nodes[p].hash_next) {\r\n99:        nodes[n].hash_next = buckets[b];\r\n123:            nodes[i].hash_next = new_buckets[b];\r\n150:        for (int p = buckets[b]; p >= 0; p = nodes[p].hash_next) {\r\nserial.c: In function ‘main’:\r\nserial.c:161:31: warning: argument 1 range [18446744065119617024, 18446744073709551608] exceeds maximum object size 9223372036854775807 \r\n[-Walloc-size-larger-than=]\r\n  161 |     char **contigs = (char **)malloc((size_t)n * sizeof(char *));\r\n      |                               ^~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~\r\nIn file included from serial.c:3:\r\n/usr/include/stdlib.h:672:14: note: in a call to allocation function ‘malloc’ declared here\r\n  672 | extern void *malloc (size_t __size) __THROW __attribute_malloc__\r\n      |              ^~~~~~\r\n--- result ---\r\n6 serial.out\r\n3590\r\n1467\r\n227\r\n3598\r\n846\r\n380\r\n"]
