[433.657439, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠹\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[433.739689, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\r\n\u001b[1;31mmini-swe-agent\u001b[0m\u001b[31m (step \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m32\u001b[0m\u001b[31m, \u001b[0m\u001b[1;31m$0.00\u001b[0m\u001b[31m):\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[433.73999, "o", "\r\u001b[2KThe parallel output is byte-for-byte identical to the serial output with 4 threads. I'll test additional thread counts, then create the required Makefile with \r\nbuild/run/verify targets.\r\n\r\n```\r\nexport PATH=/usr/local/bin:$PATH\r\ncd /app\r\nfor t in 1 2 3 8; do\r\n  echo \"=== threads $t ===\"\r\n  rm -f /app/pgen*.out\r\n  timeout 60 upcrun -n $t -shared-heap 256MB /app/pgen /app/test > /tmp/pgen_$t.log 2>&1\r\n  rc=$?\r\n  count=$(wc -l < /app/pgen_0.out 2>/dev/null || echo missing)\r\n  if cmp -s /app/serial.out /app/pgen_0.out; then eq=IDENTICAL; else eq=DIFFER; fi\r\n  echo \"rc=$rc lines=$count $eq\"\r\n  grep -E 'warning|error|ERROR' /tmp/pgen_$t.log | head -3\r\ndone\r\n```\r\n\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond..."]
[433.742454, "o", "\r\u001b[2K\u001b[32m⠸\u001b[0m Waiting for the LM to respond...\r\n\u001b[?25h\r\u001b[1A\u001b[2K"]
[438.095213, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1;32mTool\u001b[0m:\r\n"]
[438.095444, "o", "<returncode>\r\n0\r\n<output>\r\n=== threads 1 ===\r\nrc=0 lines=6 IDENTICAL\r\nUPC Runtime warning: Requested shared memory (256 MB) > available (57 MB) on node 0 (f7d7a33ec365): using 57 MB per thread instead\r\n=== threads 2 ===\r\nrc=0 lines=6 IDENTICAL\r\nUPC Runtime warning: Requested shared memory (256 MB) > available (25 MB) on node 0 (f7d7a33ec365): using 25 MB per thread instead\r\n=== threads 3 ===\r\nrc=0 lines=6 IDENTICAL\r\nUPC Runtime warning: Requested shared memory (256 MB) > available (15 MB) on node 0 (f7d7a33ec365): using 15 MB per thread instead\r\n=== threads 8 ===\r\nrc=0 lines=6 IDENTICAL\r\nUPC Runtime warning: Requested shared memory (256 MB) > available (1 MB) on node 0 (f7d7a33ec365): using 1 MB per thread instead\r\n\r\n"]
[438.100821, "o", "\u001b[92m────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[?25l"]
